This product includes software derived from imagecorruptions
(https://github.com/bethgelab/imagecorruptions), licensed under the
Apache License 2.0. The corruption functions in
src/segrobust/corruptions.py are adapted from that project, which
implements the corruption benchmark of Hendrycks & Dietterich,
"Benchmarking Neural Network Robustness to Common Corruptions and
Perturbations" (ICLR 2019). Please cite that paper when using these
corruptions in research.

The frost textures embedded in src/segrobust/frost_data.py are
PROCEDURALLY GENERATED by the segrobust project (multi-scale value noise
plus directional streaks, fixed seeds) and contain no third-party photo
content; they are licensed Apache-2.0 as part of segrobust. They replace
the photographic frost textures shipped by upstream repositories, whose
per-asset licensing is undocumented; consequently frost outputs differ
in appearance (not in algorithm) from the upstream implementation.
